==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|specific|ity}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=4215072792}}</ref> Compare {{cog|fr|spécificité}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/spɛsɪˈfɪsɪti/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-specificity.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|sensitivity and specificity}}

{{en-noun|-|+}}

# The state of being [[specific]] rather than [[general]].
#* {{quote-web|1=en|date=October 14, 2024|author=Patrick Eddington|author2=James Craven|work=Police Want the Password to Your Phone|url=https://reason.com/2024/10/14/police-want-the-password-to-your-phone/|text=Congress must set a clear standard: Police should prove with '''specificity''' what's on your phone before forcing it open, and only after the device's owner has consulted with a lawyer. Doing so would provide citizens a means to ensure police follow warrant requirements without sacrificing law enforcement's ability to pursue the crime they're investigating.}}
# The extent to which a characteristic is specific to a given person, place, or thing; thus:
## {{lb|en|statistics}} The [[probability]], in a [[binary]] [[classification]] [[test]], of a true [[negative]] being correctly identified.
##: {{coord|en|sensitivity}}
## {{lb|en|medicine}} The extent to which a particular diagnostic test is specific for, or a symptom or sign is specific to, a given condition.

